\subsection{Custom templates}{

Start from pubflow's template and keep what pubflow writes into it:
\itemize{
\item \code{reference_docx} (start from
\code{system.file("templates", "reference.docx", package = "pubflow")}):
\itemize{
\item paragraph styles "Heading 1"-"Heading 5", "Heading 1 Unnumbered"-"Heading 5
Unnumbered", "Item Title", "Table Caption", "Image Caption", "Figure" and
"Error", and the character style "Placeholder" (missing styles are added
unformatted);
\item for header and footer lines, the bookmarks \code{header_left}, \code{header_center},
\code{header_right}, \code{footer_left}, \code{footer_center} and \code{footer_right} in its header
and footer (only those of the lines you use, see \code{\link[=pub_pp_docx_header_footer]{pub_pp_docx_header_footer()}}).
}
\item \code{latex_preamble}: a file included after pubflow's header (which loads the packages
for tables, landscape pages, header and footer, and the frame of error items) and
before the document's header and footer lines.
\item \code{typst_template} (start from
\code{system.file("templates", "pubflow.typ", package = "pubflow")}): a pandoc template
that
\itemize{
\item writes \verb{$header-includes$} (page orientation and caption labels);
\item shows the title block only if \verb{$title-block$} is set;
\item takes the header and footer lines from \verb{$header-left$} to \verb{$footer-right$} (an
empty part also sets \verb{$footer-right-empty$} etc.).
}
}
}
